**Summary of additions:**
- **2 new rooms (59, 60):** Two bedrooms placed west of the existing living room (58), extending through the door (14) on Wall 36 — the door had no room defined on its far side. Room 60 sits south of room 59, forming a logical bedroom wing.
- **11 new objects**, all collision-validated (IoU = 0.0):
  - Room 53 (living room): plant
  - Room 54 (living room): bookshelf, lamp
  - Room 57 (bathroom): sink (completing the toilet/cabinet/bathtub set)
  - Room 58 (living room): plant
  - Room 59 (new bedroom): bed, nightstand, wardrobe
  - Room 60 (new bedroom): bed, dresser, nightstand

All objects respect the impassable-wall rule (none cross walls/windows without a door), avoid `nothing` and `structure` nodes, and are connected to their containing rooms. New rooms connect to each other and to the adjacent existing room via the door.
